In the service I reintroduced `conversation_id`, `self._conversation_cache_committed`, `committed_messages`, and `self._committed_cache_shape_fingerprint`; rebuilt `_build_payload()` as a client-authoritative projection over the normalized shared-context transcript; added rotation on committed-prefix rewrites and cache-shape changes; reinstated `ConversationCacheMissError` plus 409 detection and a one-shot same-`conversation_id` full-history rebase retry; and flipped historical-audio stripping default to on. Promotion of `committed_messages` now happens only after a successful request returns to `_process_context()`, never from generated assistant output.

In the bot I restored the cache env wiring: `NEMOTRON_OMNI_ENABLE_CONVERSATION_CACHE` controls whether a `conversation_id` is passed, and `NEMOTRON_OMNI_CONVERSATION_ID` overrides the generated `pipecat-...` id.

2. Current project status

